# How to cite Styx. GitHub reads this file and shows "Cite this repository" beside the code.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Styx in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Styx: a browser-based geotechnical modeller for Kratos GeoMechanics"
abstract: >-
  Styx is a single-user modeller for staged geotechnical analyses such as excavations and
  sheet pile walls. It builds the model from OpenCASCADE solids, meshes it with Gmsh, writes
  a Kratos Multiphysics GeoMechanicsApplication input deck, runs it in construction stages
  and shows the results. It can be driven from the browser or from the command line
  (kratos-cli).
authors:
  - given-names: Marjan
    family-names: Fathian
    affiliation: Deltares
repository-code: "https://github.com/Deltares-research/Styx-Kratos-GUI"
keywords:
  - geotechnical engineering
  - finite element method
  - Kratos Multiphysics
  - GeoMechanicsApplication
  - Gmsh
  - staged construction
